  "rules": "BEFORE YOU BEGIN\nChoose a banker. Each player starts with {{currency}}1,500: five 1s, one 5, two 10s, one 20, one 50, four 100s, and two 500s. Shuffle both event decks separately. Put all tokens on {{go}}.\n\nTAKE A TURN\nRoll two dice and move clockwise. Collect {{currency}}200 when you pass or land on {{go}}. Doubles let you roll again; three doubles in a row send you to {{jail}}.\n\nBUY, TRADE & BUILD\nBuy an unowned property at its printed price, or auction it among all players. Pay rent to the owner of an unmortgaged property. Owning an entire color group doubles the unimproved rent. Build evenly across a complete group: up to four houses, then replace four houses with a hotel, paying the building cost again. The bank holds 32 houses and 12 hotels.\n\nSPECIAL SPACES\nFollow event-card instructions and return used cards to the bottom of the deck, except retained cards. Pay taxes to the bank. Free parking gives no payment. On Just Visiting, take no action. In {{jail}}, pay {{currency}}50, use a release card, or try for doubles for up to three turns; after the third failed roll pay {{currency}}50 and move by that roll. A release by doubles does not give another roll.\n\nMORTGAGES & BANKRUPTCY\nSell buildings back at half cost, evenly across their group. Mortgage unimproved properties for the amount on the deed; pay that amount plus 10% to redeem. Trade mortgaged properties by agreement; the buyer pays 10% interest immediately and another 10% later if not redeemed at transfer. If you cannot pay a debt after selling and mortgaging, give remaining assets to the creditor and leave the game. If the bank is the creditor, auction the properties. The last player remaining wins.\n\nMAKE IT YOURS\nAgree on any house rules before playing. Use small objects as player tokens. Printable houses and hotels are included; fold on the dashed lines and glue the tabs."
}
